        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=8$\n\nExtend the line through $O$ to use the diameter $14$.",
          "worked": "Extend the horizontal line through $O$ to the far side of the circle. The diameter is $2\\times7=14$, so the whole horizontal secant is $6+14=20$. By the Power of a Point Theorem,\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x+7)&=6\\times20\\\\x^2+7x&=120\\\\x^2+7x-120&=0\\\\(x+15)(x-8)&=0\\\\x&=8.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $x=-15$ since a length is positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      }
